    "case_id": "556",
    "case_summary": "A 43-year-old woman with stage IV chronic kidney disease presented to the hospital with nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, abdominal pain, and altered mental status. She was being treated with cyclophosphamide, 60 mg of prednisone, and hydroxychloroquine. She had not left the United States for 14 years. Her symptoms progressively worsened with poor oral intake.\n\nVital signs on admission:- Temperature: 101.3°F- Heart rate: 110 beats per minute- Blood pressure: 107/66 mm/Hg\n\nLaboratory Tests:- Sodium level: 120 mmol/L- Creatinine level: 382 µmol/L (4.32 mg/dL)- Urinalysis: showed muddy brown casts- Stool ova and parasite: positive- Serum IgG: 2.1 g/L- Serum 1-3-β-D-glucan level: >500 pg/mL- Development of pancytopenia notedImaging Studies:- CT abdomen: showed colonic wall thickening- CT chest: demonstrated a cavitary lung lesion in the right base, later showing diffuse tree-in-bud pattern infiltrates  Image Title: Computed tomography of the chest  Image Description: Demonstrated new tree-in-bud infiltratesBronchoscopy:- Bronchoscopy findings: revealed Strongyloides filaria- Bronchoalveolar lavage: positive for Aspergillus  Image Title: Bronchoalveolar lavage findings  Image Description: Showing Strongyloides filariform larvae",
